Archaeology Story Pack 4.4

About the mod
An updated and maintained version of [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1993869579]Archaeology Story Pack for Stellaris 4.4.

The original mod added a collection of archaeology stories created by community contributors: ancient ruins, unusual worlds, relics, and narrative chains that reveal forgotten chapters of galactic history.

This version brings the mod back to the current game version while preserving its original content and making it convenient to use in a modern Stellaris mod setup.



What changed in version 4.4
• updated for the current Stellaris 4.4 version;
• compatibility with the modern game structure has been restored;
• full localizations have been added for every language officially supported by Stellaris;
• these are real translations, not copies of the English text placed into other language files;
• localization files have been unified and synchronized across all supported languages.



What the mod adds
• archaeology stories with their own narrative outcomes;
• ancient ruins, mysterious worlds, and traces of vanished civilizations;
• unique relics and special rewards;
• events tied to exploring the galaxy’s forgotten past;
• atmospheric content for campaigns where you want more discoveries, mysteries, and smaller stories between major crises.



Languages
The mod is fully localized into all 10 Stellaris languages:

• English;
• Français;
• Deutsch;
• Español;
• Polski;
• Português do Brasil;
• Русский;
• 简体中文;
• 日本語;
• 한국어.

Additional community localization:

• Français — [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3513691177]French community translation by Stern. Thanks to Stern and the French Stellaris community translators for their work.



Compatibility
This version is made for Stellaris 4.4.

The original Archaeology Story Pack did not overwrite vanilla files, so it was compatible with most mods in theory; this version preserves the same approach.

The mod works well alongside other event and exploration mods, as well as Planetary Diversity and All These Worlds - Lite.

Important compatibility note:
I do not recommend using this mod together with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=727000451]More Events Mod.

The authors of More Events Mod have added the content of Archaeology Story Pack directly into their own mod. Because of that, using both mods at the same time may lead to compatibility problems, such as missing localization, duplicated dig sites, duplicated events, or other unexpected issues.

If you use More Events Mod, you probably do not need this mod enabled at the same time.



Important
This is an updated version of an older mod, created to preserve its functionality on the current game version.

If you are using the old [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1993869579]Archaeology Story Pack or earlier continuation versions, keep only one version of the mod enabled.



Credits
Thanks to the authors of the original [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1993869579]Archaeology Story Pack — XVCV, 슈팅스타, and ChupaChups — for the mod and its stories.

Thanks as well to Inny for the later continuation [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3079374348]Archaeology Story Pack 4.2, which helped keep the mod available to players after support for the original version ended.



Support
If you notice a bug, a broken chain, an untranslated line, or a compatibility issue with the current game version, please leave a comment and I will check it.

If you enjoy the mod and would like to support its further development, please leave a positive rating and add it to your favorites. Thank you for your trust and support!

This mods adds option to play as machine empire for custom races available in mod United Sci-Fi Races. It adds more robotic/cyborg races to Machine section. The mod requires [url=http://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=814332008] United Sci-Fi races  and SD DLC.

It is made as a patch since it alters ...common\species_classes00_species_classes.txt. Unfortenatly, this is the only way I easely found to make work mechanics of SD for custom races.

In case you think that it is more organic than robotic you can always select the same portrait from base Sci-Fi races sections. To create machine empire you must select portrait from section Machine.

Following races included: 
• Doctor Who: cybermen, daleks;
• Halo: huragok, Cortana, prometheans;
• Mass Effect: EDI, geths, reapers, collectors, remnants;
• Star Trek: borgs;
• Star Wars: robots;
• Warhammer 40,000: necrons;
• Other: terminators, cylons from Battlestar Galactica;
• Special Stellaris races: 2 versions of The Contingency and variations of robots.
• Fantasy: robotic 2 races 

Only default + extended robots are randomised while other sci-fi specific robots will not be randomly spawned /generated.

